  'cape-town-may-bring-in-water-restrictions-from-december-2026-10-23',
  'Cape Town weighs precautionary water restrictions from December',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-23', 'Cape Town Etc', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/cape-town-could-face-water-restrictions-as-dam-levels-fall-ahead-of-summer/',
  'Cape Town may bring in precautionary water restrictions around December as dams keep falling, though no final decision has been made.',
  'Cape Town may introduce precautionary water restrictions at about the start of December, with storage in the Western Cape Water Supply System continues to slip and daily consumption sits above the City''s target. Reports say the timing is not yet a final decision.

The possibility came up when City officials recently met the national water department. Cape Town Etc reports that the City''s bulk services director wants more assessments completed before farming-sector limits are fixed. The department is expected to run more modelling, and the City must complete its own processes before it can introduce restrictions that apply locally.

The Water and Sanitation mayoral committee member has said the City is monitoring rainfall, dam levels and consumption closely and taking a cautious approach. The City''s 2026 Water Outlook shows no immediate threat to supply, but the risk of restrictions is higher than in previous years, particularly if demand stays high or the rains fall short. To lower that risk, the City wants dams to be at 80% or better when the wet season closes. Further assessments are due in late October and early November, with an outcome expected to be communicated early in November.

Residents are being urged to cut unnecessary use now. The City notes that most high-volume water use happens at home, and asks people to fix leaking taps and toilets, take shorter showers, avoid unnecessary hosepipe use, water gardens efficiently and reuse suitable water where possible.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
